  "assumptions": [
    "Mumbai wind and seismic site proxy; confirm the wind isotach and zone at 19.30 N, 73.06 E.",
    "Site soil Type II pending geotechnical confirmation.",
    "Trial connection details and matched source member checks are recorded where available. Each unverified design item retains review status.",
    "Rooflight openings and separate translucent sheets occupy 3% of the gross main roof in plan and on the slope. Producer design uses a 1.5 mm polycarbonate envelope allowance; the supplier confirms sheet grade, curb and trimmer details, fall protection, overlaps, fasteners and watertight seals.",
    "The endwall sheeting is set on outward-facing IS 811 Z rails. Remaining triangular verge infill, local corner closure, lap lengths, gable cleats and cladding fasteners require envelope detailing.",
    "Continuous ridge ventilation is a specialist envelope package. Opening width, curb, flashing, local trimming and rain exclusion require the ventilator supplier specification.",
    "The 50 mm roof insulation is included in roof dead load. The envelope supplier coordinates the thermal blanket, standing seam or profiled liner, spacers and sealed rooflight transitions.",
    "Twenty 3.0 x 3.5 m east dock openings and four 6 x 6 m gable openings are set out between columns. Dock-leveller pits, equipment, edge beams, anchors and manufacturer reactions belong to equipment and foundation coordination.",
    "The 230 mm masonry dado bears on its own plinth. Its out-of-plane ties, foundation and movement joints require local masonry and foundation detailing.",
    "Portal eave and ridge values are fixed structural workline elevations. Across the main roof the inner skin is 792.0 mm vertically above that datum. The long façade is 791.0 mm outside the column grid. Roof and long-wall packing varies from 16.0 to 166.0 mm. The gable and door jamb attachments, outer cladding fixings, water seals and thermal movement require envelope-supplier details."
  ],
